"""One glossary for lessons (term chips, Words to know, Glossary tab) and videos (term cards + spoken definitions).
Each entry: key, term shown, spoken form, plain meaning, everyday analogy, optional text regex (rx) and speech regex (sx).
Meanings and analogies avoid other acronyms so each card stands on its own."""
import re
G=[]
def T(k,term,say,mean,ana,rx=None,sx=None,full=None,ci=False):
    G.append(dict(k=k,t=term,say=say,mean=mean,ana=ana,rx=rx,sx=sx,full=full,ci=ci))
# ---- USB device side
T('udc','UDC','U D C','USB Device Controller: the chip block that lets a gadget answer a laptop over USB.','The front desk of a hotel: every guest request (the laptop) arrives there first.',full='device controller')
T('dwc3','DWC3 (Synopsys IP)','D W C 3','A ready-made USB controller design that Synopsys sells and many Qualcomm and NXP chips include.','A front desk bought from a furniture catalogue: many hotels have the same model, so one driver fits them all.',rx=r'\bDWC3\b|DesignWare',sx=r'\b[Dd] [Ww] [Cc] (?:3|three)\b|\bDWC3\b|DesignWare')
T('gadget','Gadget (Linux USB gadget)','gadget','Linux\'s name for the device side of USB: the board pretends to be a webcam, mic or keyboard to a laptop.','An actor in costume: the same board can play "webcam" or "keyboard" depending on the costume it wears.',rx=r'\b[Gg]adget\b',sx=r'\b[Gg]adget\b')
T('configfs','configfs','config F S','A special folder tree where you build a USB gadget by creating folders and writing small files.','Building with LEGO by making folders: each folder is a brick (a function), and linking them snaps the toy together.',rx=r'\bconfigfs\b',sx=r'\bconfig ?[Ff] ?[Ss]\b|\bconfigfs\b')
T('functionfs','FunctionFS','function F S','A way for a normal program, not kernel code, to implement one USB function of a gadget.','Letting a contractor run one counter of the shop instead of hiring a full-time employee.',rx=r'\bFunctionFS\b',sx=r'\b[Ff]unction ?[Ff] ?[Ss]\b|FunctionFS')
T('composite','Composite device','composite','One USB device that offers several functions at once, like camera plus mic plus buttons.','A multi-tool: one handle, several blades.',rx=r'\bcomposite\b',sx=r'\bcomposite\b',ci=True)
T('uvc','UVC','U V C','USB Video Class: the standard "I am a webcam" language every computer already understands.','A universal power plug for cameras: plug in anywhere and it just works, no driver install.')
T('uac','UAC / UAC2','U A C','USB Audio Class (version 2 is the modern one): the standard "I am a mic or speaker" language.','The same universal plug idea as the webcam language, but for sound.',rx=r'\bUAC[123]?\b',sx=r'\b[Uu] [Aa] [Cc]\b|\bUAC[123]?\b')
T('hid','HID','H I D','Human Interface Device: the standard language for buttons, keyboards and mice, also used for mute and call buttons.','The universal remote-control language: any computer knows what "button pressed" means.')
T('cdc','CDC / ACM','C D C','Communications Device Class: a standard USB serial port or network link, handy for debug consoles.','A walkie-talkie channel built into the cable for engineers to talk to the device.',rx=r'\bCDC\b|\bACM\b',sx=r'\b[Cc] [Dd] [Cc]\b|\bCDC\b|\b[Aa] [Cc] [Mm]\b')
T('mtp','MTP','M T P','Media Transfer Protocol: how a phone shows its photos as files on a computer.','A librarian handing you books one at a time instead of letting you into the stacks.')
T('xhci','xHCI','x H C I','Extensible Host Controller Interface: the standard USB host controller in laptops and in our boards when they act as host.','The hotel manager who calls guests, as opposed to the front desk that answers them.',rx=r'\bxHCI\b',sx=r'\b[Xx] [Hh] [Cc] [Ii]\b|\bxHCI\b')
T('endpoint','Endpoint','endpoint','A numbered mailbox on a USB device; each data stream uses its own.','Numbered pigeonholes in an office: mail for video goes in one slot, audio in another.',rx=r'\b[Ee]ndpoints?\b',sx=r'\b[Ee]ndpoints?\b')
T('descriptor','Descriptor','descriptor','A small table of facts the device reports about itself: who made it, what it can do.','A business card plus resume the device hands over when it is first plugged in.',rx=r'\b[Dd]escriptors?\b',sx=r'\b[Dd]escriptors?\b')
T('enum','Enumeration','enumeration','The first conversation after plug-in where the laptop learns what the device is and gives it an address.','A new employee\'s first morning: show ID, get a badge number, hand in a resume, get assigned a desk.',rx=r'\b[Ee]numerat\w*',sx=r'\b[Ee]numerat\w*')
T('isoc','Isochronous transfer','isochronous','A USB transfer type with guaranteed timing but no retries, used for live video and audio.','A live TV broadcast: always on time, and a dropped frame is simply skipped, never resent.',rx=r'\b[Ii]sochronous\b|\bisoc\b',sx=r'\b[Ii]sochronous\b')
T('bulk','Bulk transfer','bulk transfer','A USB transfer type that is reliable but has no timing promise, used for files and updates.','Parcel post: everything arrives intact, but not at a promised minute.',rx=r'\b[Bb]ulk\b',sx=r'\b[Bb]ulk\b')
T('setup','SETUP packet / control transfer','setup packet','The eight-byte question the host sends on endpoint zero to start every control conversation.','The short form you fill in at a counter before anything else happens.',rx=r'\bSETUP\b|control transfer',sx=r'\b[Ss]etup packet|control transfer')
T('stall','STALL','stall','The device\'s way of saying "I can\'t do that request."','A clerk holding up a hand: "not at this counter."',rx=r'\bSTALL\b',sx=r'\b[Ss]tall(?:s|ed)?\b')
T('vbus','VBUS','V bus','The 5-volt power wire in a USB cable; seeing it tells the device a host is attached.','The doorbell wire: when it carries power, someone is at the door.',rx=r'\bVBUS\b',sx=r'\b[Vv] ?bus\b|\bVBUS\b')
T('drd','DRD / OTG','D R D','Dual-role device: one USB port that can switch between being host and being device.','A person who can be either the customer or the shopkeeper depending on who walks in.',rx=r'\bDRD\b|\bOTG\b',sx=r'\b[Dd] [Rr] [Dd]\b|\bDRD\b|\b[Oo] [Tt] [Gg]\b')
T('phy','PHY','phy','The physical-layer circuit that turns bits into electrical signals on the wire.','The voice box that turns your thoughts into sound waves.',rx=r'\bPHY\b',sx=r'\b[Pp] [Hh] [Yy]\b|\bPHY\b|\bphy\b')
T('typec','USB Type-C','Type C','The reversible USB connector; it also negotiates power and roles through its extra pins.','A smart socket that works either way up and agrees on who powers whom before turning on.',rx=r'\bType-C\b',sx=r'\bType[ -]C\b')
T('pd','PD (Power Delivery)','P D','USB Power Delivery: the conversation over the Type-C cable that agrees on voltage, current and roles.','Two people agreeing how much to pay before handing over goods.',rx=r'\bPD\b',sx=r'\bP D\b|\bPD\b|[Pp]ower [Dd]elivery')
T('cc','CC pins','C C','The configuration-channel wires in a Type-C cable used to detect orientation and talk Power Delivery.','The cable\'s private phone line for negotiating before the main road opens.',rx=r'\bCC[12]?\b',sx=r'\bC C\b|\bCC[12]?\b')
T('altmode','Alternate mode','alternate mode','Using some Type-C wires to carry another signal, such as DisplayPort video, instead of USB data.','A multi-lane road where some lanes are temporarily given to buses.',rx=r'\b[Aa]lternate modes?\b|\bAlt[ -]?mode',sx=r'\b[Aa]lternate modes?\b')
T('dfu','DFU','D F U','Device Firmware Upgrade: a standard way to send new firmware into a device over USB.','A car driving onto a service ramp so the mechanic can swap the engine software.')
T('usbmon','usbmon','USB mon','A Linux feature that records every USB packet so you can read them in Wireshark.','A security camera pointed at the USB cable.',rx=r'\busbmon\b',sx=r'\b[Uu][Ss][Bb] ?mon\b|\bU S B mon\b')
T('urb','URB','U R B','USB Request Block: the kernel\'s envelope for one USB transfer request on the host side.','A filled-in courier slip attached to each package.')
T('lpm','LPM / U1 / U2','L P M','Link power management: USB links nap between packets to save power.','Lights on a motion sensor that switch off when the hallway is empty.',rx=r'\bLPM\b|\bU[12]\b',sx=r'\b[Ll] [Pp] [Mm]\b|\bLPM\b|\b[Uu] ?(?:one|two)\b(?= and| or| states)')
# ---- Android
T('hal','HAL','HAL','Hardware Abstraction Layer: a fixed interface Android calls, which the device maker implements for its hardware.','A standard wall socket: Android plugs into the same socket, and each maker wires the house behind it.',rx=r'\bHALs?\b',sx=r'\bHALs?\b|\b[Hh] [Aa] [Ll]\b',full='hardware abstraction layer')
T('aidl','AIDL','A I D L','Android Interface Definition Language: the file that describes the calls between two Android processes.','A menu both the waiter and the kitchen agree on, so orders are never misunderstood.',rx=r'\bAIDL\b',sx=r'\b[Aa] [Ii] [Dd] [Ll]\b|\bAIDL\b')
T('hidl','HIDL','hidle','The older Android interface language that AIDL replaced for hardware services.','Last year\'s menu format, still found in older restaurants.')
T('treble','Treble','Treble','Android\'s split between Google\'s system part and the vendor\'s hardware part, so each can update separately.','A building with a fixed wall between the landlord\'s floors and the tenant\'s floors.',rx=r'\bTreble\b',sx=r'\bTreble\b')
T('gki','GKI','G K I','Generic Kernel Image: one Google-built Linux kernel shared by many devices, with vendor drivers loaded as modules.','A standard car chassis from the factory, with each brand bolting on its own parts.')
T('vintf','VINTF','vintf','The vendor interface manifest: the list that says which hardware services a device provides.','A restaurant\'s posted list of dishes it promises to serve.')
T('selinux','SELinux','S E Linux','Security-Enhanced Linux: rules that say exactly which program may touch which file or device, even as root.','Keycards in an office: even the boss\'s card only opens the doors it is programmed for.',rx=r'\bSELinux\b',sx=r'\b[Ss] ?[Ee] ?Linux\b|\bSELinux\b')
T('init','init / .rc files','init','The first user program Android starts; its .rc files say which services start and when.','The stage manager with a script that says who walks on stage and when.',rx=r'\binit\.rc\b|\.rc\b|\binit\b',sx=r'\binit\b(?! ?ram)')
T('aosp','AOSP','A O S P','Android Open Source Project: the public Android source code a device maker builds from.','The public recipe book every Android kitchen starts from.')
T('adb','adb','A D B','Android Debug Bridge: the command-line tool that gives an engineer a shell and logs on a device.','A service hatch into the device for the technician.',rx=r'\badb\b|\bADB\b',sx=r'\b[Aa] [Dd] [Bb]\b|\badb\b')
T('cts','CTS / VTS','C T S','Android\'s Compatibility and Vendor Test Suites, which a device must pass to ship with Google apps.','The driving test every new car model must pass before it can be sold.',rx=r'\bCTS\b|\bVTS\b',sx=r'\b[CcVv] [Tt] [Ss]\b|\bCTS\b|\bVTS\b')
T('framework','Framework layer','framework layer','On Android, the Java system services apps talk to, like the camera and USB services.','The dining room of a restaurant: diners (apps) only ever see this room.',rx=r'\b[Ff]ramework\b',sx=r'\b[Ff]ramework\b')
# ---- Linux kernel and drivers
T('kernel','Kernel','kernel','The core of the operating system that controls memory, devices and which program runs.','The building manager who owns every key and decides who uses which room.',rx=r'\b[Kk]ernel\b',sx=r'\b[Kk]ernel\b')
T('driver','Driver','driver','Kernel code that knows how to operate one kind of hardware.','A translator who speaks one specific machine\'s language.',rx=r'\b[Dd]rivers?\b',sx=r'\b[Dd]rivers?\b')
T('firmware','Firmware','firmware','Software that runs close to hardware, usually stored in flash memory on the device.','The instincts built into an animal: low-level behaviour that is there from birth.',rx=r'\b[Ff]irmware\b',sx=r'\b[Ff]irmware\b')
T('userspace','User space','user space','Where normal programs run, outside the kernel, protected from crashing the whole system.','The public area of a building, separate from the staff-only control room.',rx=r'\b[Uu]ser ?space\b',sx=r'\b[Uu]ser ?space\b')
T('module','Kernel module','kernel module','A piece of kernel code that can be loaded or removed while the system runs.','A plug-in cartridge for a game console.',rx=r'\b[Kk]ernel modules?\b|\.ko\b|\binsmod\b',sx=r'\b[Kk]ernel modules?\b')
T('probe','probe()','probe','The driver function the kernel calls when it finds a device that matches the driver.','The first handshake when a translator is introduced to the person they will translate for.',rx=r'\bprobe\(\)|\bprobe\b',sx=r'\b[Pp]robe\b')
T('dt','Device tree','device tree','A text map of the hardware on a board (which chips, on which pins and addresses) that the kernel reads at boot.','The floor plan of a house, so the electrician knows where every socket is without digging into walls.',rx=r'\b[Dd]evice [Tt]ree\b|\bDT\b|\bDTS\b',sx=r'\b[Dd]evice [Tt]ree\b')
T('dtb','DTB / overlay','D T B','The compiled, binary form of the device tree that the bootloader hands to the kernel; an overlay patches it.','The printed floor plan; an overlay is a sticky note added on top.',rx=r'\bDTBO?\b|\b[Oo]verlays?\b',sx=r'\b[Dd] [Tt] [Bb]\b|\bDTB\b|\b[Oo]verlays?\b')
T('i2c','I2C','I two C','A simple two-wire bus that lets a processor talk to small chips like sensors and HDMI bridges.','A classroom where the teacher calls each student by number and they answer one at a time.',rx=r'\bI2C\b',sx=r'\bI two C\b|\bI2C\b|\bi two c\b')
T('spi','SPI','S P I','A fast four-wire bus for chips like flash memory and displays.','A dedicated phone line to each chip instead of a shared classroom.',rx=r'\bSPI\b',sx=r'\b[Ss] [Pp] [Ii]\b|\bSPI\b')
T('gpio','GPIO','G P I O','General-purpose input/output: a single pin software can switch on or off, or read.','A light switch the software can flip or check.',rx=r'\bGPIOs?\b',sx=r'\b[Gg] [Pp] [Ii] [Oo]\b|\bGPIO\b')
T('uart','UART','U art','A simple serial port, often the first console you see when a board boots.','A tin-can telephone straight into the board.',rx=r'\bUART\b',sx=r'\b[Uu] ?art\b|\bUART\b')
T('regmap','regmap','reg map','A kernel helper that reads and writes a chip\'s registers over I2C or SPI with caching.','A shared notebook of a chip\'s settings so you do not re-ask the chip every time.',rx=r'\bregmap\b',sx=r'\breg ?map\b')
T('mmio','MMIO / register','M M I O','Memory-mapped input/output: hardware settings that appear as memory addresses the processor writes to.','Dials on a control panel that happen to be numbered like house addresses.',rx=r'\bMMIO\b',sx=r'\b[Mm] [Mm] [Ii] [Oo]\b|\bMMIO\b')
T('irq','IRQ / interrupt','I R Q','Interrupt request: a hardware signal that makes the processor stop and handle an event right now.','A doorbell: you stop what you are doing and answer it.',rx=r'\bIRQs?\b|\b[Ii]nterrupts?\b',sx=r'\b[Ii] [Rr] [Qq]s?\b|\bIRQs?\b|\b[Ii]nterrupts?\b')
T('isr','ISR / top half','I S R','Interrupt service routine: the tiny, fast handler that runs the moment the interrupt fires.','Answering the doorbell just long enough to take the parcel.',rx=r'\bISRs?\b|\btop half\b',sx=r'\b[Ii] [Ss] [Rr]\b|\bISR\b|\btop half\b')
T('workqueue','Workqueue / bottom half','workqueue','A kernel queue that runs deferred work later in a normal context where sleeping is allowed.','Putting the parcel on the table to open properly after you have closed the door.',rx=r'\b[Ww]orkqueues?\b|\bbottom half\b',sx=r'\b[Ww]ork ?queues?\b|\bbottom half\b')
T('threadedirq','Threaded IRQ','threaded I R Q','An interrupt whose slow part runs in its own kernel thread so it can sleep and talk over I2C.','A receptionist who takes a message, then a colleague phones back properly.',rx=r'\b[Tt]hreaded IRQs?\b|request_threaded_irq',sx=r'\b[Tt]hreaded (?:I R Q|IRQ|interrupt)s?\b')
T('dma','DMA','D M A','Direct memory access: a hardware helper that copies data to memory without the processor doing each byte.','A conveyor belt that moves boxes while the worker does something else.',rx=r'\bDMA\b|\bdma-buf\b',sx=r'\b[Dd] [Mm] [Aa]\b|\bDMA\b')
T('spinlock','Spinlock / mutex','spinlock','Locks that stop two pieces of code changing the same data at once; a spinlock waits busily, a mutex sleeps.','A single bathroom key: a spinlock is waiting at the door, a mutex is taking a seat until called.',rx=r'\b[Ss]pinlocks?\b|\b[Mm]utex(?:es)?\b',sx=r'\b[Ss]pin ?locks?\b|\b[Mm]utex(?:es)?\b')
T('sysfs','sysfs / ioctl','sys F S','Ways a program talks to a driver: sysfs files for simple settings, ioctl calls for commands.','Labelled switches on the wall (sysfs) and a request form at the counter (ioctl).',rx=r'\bsysfs\b|\bioctl\b',sx=r'\bsys ?[Ff] ?[Ss]\b|\bsysfs\b|\bI O control\b|\bioctl\b')
T('v4l2','V4L2','V four L two','Video for Linux 2: the kernel interface every Linux camera and video device uses.','The standard loading dock every camera truck backs into.',rx=r'\bV4L2\b|Video4Linux2',sx=r'\b[Vv] four [Ll] two\b|\b[Vv]ideo for Linux\b|\bV4L2\b')
T('mc','Media controller','media controller','A kernel interface that describes and connects the blocks of a camera pipeline (sensor, image processor, outputs).','A train-yard map with switch levers you set before the train runs.',rx=r'\b[Mm]edia controller\b',sx=r'\b[Mm]edia controller\b')
T('alsa','ALSA / ASoC','ALSA','Advanced Linux Sound Architecture: the kernel\'s audio system; ASoC is its part for chips on boards.','The plumbing that carries sound from microphones to programs and back to speakers.',rx=r'\bALSA\b|\bASoC\b',sx=r'\bALSA\b|\b[Aa] ?[Ss]o[Cc]\b|\bA S o C\b')
T('isp','ISP','I S P','Image signal processor: the chip block that turns raw sensor data into a good-looking picture.','A photo lab that develops the raw film into a finished print.',rx=r'\bISP\b',sx=r'\b[Ii] [Ss] [Pp]\b|\bISP\b')
T('csi','MIPI CSI','C S I','The fast camera interface between an image sensor and the processor.','A dedicated pipe from the camera eye to the brain.',rx=r'\bCSI\b',sx=r'\b[Cc] [Ss] [Ii]\b|\bCSI\b')
T('yuv','YUY2 / NV12 / MJPEG','pixel formats','Ways to pack image pixels: brightness and colour stored separately (YUY2, NV12) or compressed per frame (MJPEG).','Different ways to pack a suitcase: rolled, folded, or vacuum-sealed.',rx=r'\bYUY2\b|\bNV12\b|\bMJPEG\b|\bYUYV\b',sx=r'\b[Yy] [Uu] [Yy] (?:2|two)\b|\bYUY2\b|\b[Nn] [Vv] (?:12|twelve)\b|\bM ?J ?P ?E ?G\b')
# ---- Boot and build
T('soc','SoC','S o C','System on a chip: one chip holding the processor cores, graphics, video, USB and more.','A whole city on one island: houses, factories and roads in one place.',rx=r'\bSoCs?\b',sx=r'\b[Ss] [Oo] [Cc]\b|\bSoC\b|\b[Ss]ystem on (?:a )?chip')
T('bsp','BSP','B S P','Board Support Package: the chip vendor\'s bundle of bootloader, kernel, drivers and settings for one chip or board.','The starter kit that comes with a new appliance: parts, manual and tools for that exact model.',rx=r'\bBSPs?\b',sx=r'\b[Bb] [Ss] [Pp]\b|\bBSP\b',full='board support package')
T('bootloader','Bootloader','bootloader','The small program that runs first at power-on, sets up memory and loads the kernel.','The stagehand who sets up the stage before the actors arrive.',rx=r'\b[Bb]ootloaders?\b',sx=r'\b[Bb]oot ?loaders?\b')
T('uboot','U-Boot / ABL / XBL','U boot','Common bootloaders: U-Boot on many boards; ABL and XBL on Qualcomm chips.','Different brands of stagehand, each with its own checklist.',rx=r'\bU-Boot\b|\bABL\b|\bXBL\b',sx=r'\bU-Boot\b|\bU [Bb]oot\b|\b[Aa] [Bb] [Ll]\b|\b[Xx] [Bb] [Ll]\b')
T('rom','Boot ROM','boot ROM','Code burned into the chip at the factory that runs first and checks the next stage.','The building\'s foundation stone: cannot be changed and everything rests on it.',rx=r'\b[Bb]oot ?ROM\b|\bROM\b',sx=r'\b[Bb]oot ?ROM\b|\b[Bb]oot rom\b')
T('secureboot','Secure boot / chain of trust','secure boot','Each boot stage checks the digital signature of the next before running it.','Each guard checks the next guard\'s badge before handing over the keys.',rx=r'\b[Ss]ecure boot\b|\bchain of trust\b',sx=r'\b[Ss]ecure boot\b|\bchain of trust\b')
T('tee','TEE / TF-A','T E E','Trusted execution environment: a walled-off secure world on the processor for keys and secrets.','A bank vault inside the building that even the building manager cannot enter.',rx=r'\bTEE\b|\bTF-A\b|\bBL31\b',sx=r'\b[Tt] [Ee] [Ee]\b|\bTEE\b')
T('avb','AVB / dm-verity','A V B','Android Verified Boot and dm-verity: checks that the system partitions have not been changed, block by block.','A tamper seal on every page of the rulebook.',rx=r'\bAVB\b|\bdm-verity\b',sx=r'\b[Aa] [Vv] [Bb]\b|\bAVB\b|\bd m verity\b|\bdm-verity\b')
T('ab','A/B partitions','A B slots','Two copies of the system; update the idle one and switch, falling back if the new one fails.','Two identical stages: rehearse on one while the show runs on the other.',rx=r'\bA/B\b',sx=r'\bA ?/ ?B\b|\bA B (?:slots?|partitions?|update)')
T('yocto','Yocto / BitBake','Yocto','A build system that compiles a whole custom Linux image from recipes; BitBake is its build engine.','A bakery that follows recipe cards to bake a whole custom cake from scratch.',rx=r'\bYocto\b|\bBitBake\b|\bbitbake\b',sx=r'\bYocto\b|\b[Bb]it ?[Bb]ake\b')
T('buildroot','Buildroot','Buildroot','A simpler build system that makes a small Linux image from one configuration menu.','A meal kit: fewer choices, but dinner is ready fast.',rx=r'\bBuildroot\b',sx=r'\b[Bb]uild ?root\b')
T('qemu','QEMU','kew em you','A program that emulates a whole computer, so you can test kernels without real hardware.','A flight simulator for software.',rx=r'\bQEMU\b',sx=r'\bQEMU\b|\b[Kk]ew ?[Ee]m[u ]|\bQ ?E ?M ?U\b')
# ---- Media
T('codec','Codec','codec','Software or hardware that compresses and decompresses video or audio.','Vacuum-packing clothes for travel, then unpacking them at the hotel.',rx=r'\b[Cc]odecs?\b',sx=r'\b[Cc]odecs?\b')
T('h264','H.264 / H.265','H two sixty four','Standard video compression formats; H.265 needs about half the bits of H.264 for the same quality.','Two generations of vacuum-packing: the newer one squeezes tighter.',rx=r'\bH\.26[45]\b|\bHEVC\b|\bAVC\b',sx=r'\bH two sixty (?:four|five)\b|\bH\.26[45]\b')
T('iframe','I-frame / keyframe','I frame','A complete picture in a video stream; the frames between only store changes.','A full photo every so often, with sticky notes of changes in between.',rx=r'\bI-frames?\b|\b[Kk]ey ?frames?\b|\bIDR\b|\bGOP\b',sx=r'\bI[- ]frames?\b|\b[Kk]ey ?frames?\b|\bI D R\b')
T('svc','SVC','S V C','Scalable Video Coding: video sent in layers so a slow receiver can drop layers instead of the whole picture.','A layered cake: a guest with little appetite takes just the bottom layer.',rx=r'\bSVC\b',sx=r'\b[Ss] [Vv] [Cc]\b|\bSVC\b',full='scalable video coding')
T('hdmi','HDMI','H D M I','The common cable standard for sending video and audio to TVs and monitors.','A garden hose for pictures and sound.',rx=r'\bHDMI\b',sx=r'\b[Hh] [Dd] [Mm] [Ii]\b|\bHDMI\b')
T('edid','EDID / HPD','E D I D','EDID is the screen\'s description of what it can show; hot-plug detect (HPD) is the wire that says a screen is connected.','A guest\'s dietary card (EDID) and the doorbell that says they arrived (HPD).',rx=r'\bEDID\b|\bHPD\b',sx=r'\b[Ee] [Dd] [Ii] [Dd]\b|\bEDID\b|\b[Hh] [Pp] [Dd]\b|\b[Hh]ot ?plug')
T('hdcp','HDCP','H D C P','A copy-protection handshake on video links.','A ticket check at the cinema door.')
T('drm','DRM / KMS','D R M','The Linux display system (Direct Rendering Manager) that drives screens and outputs.','The stage lighting desk that decides what appears on each screen.',rx=r'\bDRM\b|\bKMS\b',sx=r'\b[Dd] [Rr] [Mm]\b|\bDRM\b')
# ---- MCU, debug, quality, network
